Twenty-four teams compete in the league – eighteen returning teams from the previous season, two teams relegated from [[2024–25 EFL League Two|EFL League Two]], two teams promoted from the [[2024–25 National League#National League North|National League North]] and two teams promoted from the [[2024–25 National League#National League South|National League South]].

[[Morecambe F.C.|Morecambe]] were suspended in July 2025 after the club failed to reach a deadline on their finances to the league, with their opening fixtures in the competition postponed.<ref name=NL28Jul>{{cite web |date=28 July 2025 |title=National League Statement: Morecambe FC |url=https://www.thenationalleague.org.uk/national-league-statement-morecambe-fc-83855 |accessdate=28 July 2025 |website=www.thenationalleague.org.uk}}</ref><ref name="BBC28Jul2025">{{cite web |date=28 July 2025 |title=Morecambe suspended from the National League |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/crlz899y883o |accessdate=28 July 2025 |publisher=BBC Sport}}</ref> The club's suspension was lifted three weeks later after the club was taken over by the Panjab Warriors consortium, allowing them to take part.<ref>{{cite web |title=Morecambe's National League suspension lifted as takeover confirmed |url=https://www.msn.com/en-us/sports/other/morecambes-national-league-suspension-lifted-as-takeover-confirmed/ar-AA1KGIpe |website=MSN |publisher=ESPN |date=17 July 2025 |access-date=20 January 2026}}</ref> On the final match day the top 2 teams [[Rochdale A.F.C.|Rochdale]] and [[York City F.C.|York City]] played each other in a game where the winner won the [[National League (division)|National League]]. In that game Rochdale scored in the 96th minute, only for York City to equalize in the 106th. 

